  "body": "The post gate's rapid-in-stock law now judges radial (cross-drill) programs (#79, found by #77).\n\n**Why it was off**: M5.2 F2 switched the check off for `Mode::Radial` - the mill check reads stock as columns from above, so a retract sliding out of its own sideways hole looked like a rapid through solid stock; the gate then trusted the cross-drill planner's own promise and was blind (a station-change rapid 5 mm inside uncut stock posted with no warning).\n\n**What changed**\n- New `crates/sim/src/verify/rapids_radial.rs` (188 lines); `rapids.rs` routes `Mode::Radial` there instead of skipping it.\n- The tool is the drill's cutting length as discs of radius `r - gouge_tol` square to the tool, at the tip and every 1 mm back along the flutes, sampled at most 0.5 mm apart along each rapid with the controller's interpolated orientation (`midpose::intervals`).\n- Stock = the stock outline (or the region) under the stock top, unbounded below - the mill check's stock.\n- Rapids may pass through material earlier cuts removed (a tool-radius cylinder around each earlier cut, extended along the tool by the cutting length for straight plunges): retracts up a just-drilled hole and peck chip-breaks are clean; a rapid down a hole not yet drilled, or through uncut stock, blocks as `RapidInStock { at }`.\n\n**A real collision caught at once**: `drilling_cross`'s 44 mm box-stock fixture - the approach (move 0) stops inside the box, the slide between holes (move 6) passes through it. That is the #77 bug (PR #82). `a_cross_drill_op_runs_clean_in_the_document` moved onto a bar-sized `bar_stock_world` so it still tests what it was written for; new `a_rapid_inside_the_raw_box_stock_never_posts_silently` asserts every rapid its own geometry finds inside the box is named and blocks the post (vacuous once #82 lands - it won't break then).\n\n**Pinned by** `radial_rapids::{a_station_change_hopped_outside_the_stock_is_clean, a_station_change_chord_through_the_stock_blocks_by_name, the_column_reading_still_stands_for_a_mill_mode_twin, an_approach_that_stops_inside_the_stock_blocks, a_rapid_down_a_hole_not_yet_drilled_blocks, peck_chip_breaks_and_the_full_retract_ride_the_kerf, a_lateral_slide_out_of_the_hole_blocks, the_over_the_end_face_detour_is_clean_and_a_low_one_blocks}` + `drilling_cross::a_rapid_inside_the_raw_box_stock_never_posts_silently`.\n\n**Gates**: quick gate green; the agent ran camcraft-sim, verify 21, drilling_cross 10, drilling_axial 7, posting 17, rotary_verify 9, rotary_fixtures 4, turning 5, lathe_post 5, conformance 5, clippy -D warnings - green.\n\n**Not covered** (as in the mill check): shank/holder vs stock along a rapid; the stock is unbounded below.\n\nChangelog: fix(sim): the post gate's rapid-in-stock law now judges radial (cross-drill) programs against the raw stock - a rapid through uncut stock is named RapidInStock and blocks the post; retracts up a drilled hole stay clean\n\nFixes #79\n",
